      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, stacking pallets in Rotterdam, you say? Well, it's like trying to balance a whole bunch of mischievous goblins on a tightrope. You want to keep those goblins (or in your case, pallets) in a way that they don't topple over and cause a ruckus. So, first things first, think of your center of gravity as the tightrope itself. You don't want it to sway too much, or you'll have a disaster on your hands. Place your heaviest loads at the bottom, like the sturdy, burly goblins who don't mind getting their hands dirty. As you stack upwards, gradually lighten the load, like giving the smaller, lighter goblins a chance to play without fear of falling off the tightrope.\n\nNow, about those interlocking patterns, imagine you're trying to keep a group of goblins from wandering off. You want them to stick together, right? So, when you're stacking, make sure each pallet is snugly fitted with the one below it. This way, they're all holding hands, so to speak, and won't stray too far from the group. And remember, just like with goblins, it's all about balance and keeping everyone in their place. Good luck with your",
